## 6. Existing finite consumer and unresolved quantifiers

The actual allowance (3.3) is an independent input to [Multiword, Theorem 3.1][MW], whose statistic, response theorem and finite detectability result are reused. For the same fixed row-unifilar candidate $P$, take $C=[1,L]$, $f_C=f(X_C)$, $F=\max_{B_L}|f|$, and require

$$
\mathbb E_P[f_C\mid\sigma(X_j:j\notin C)]=0.
$$

Write $q_i=\mathbb E_P[X_i\mid\sigma(X_j:j\ne i)]$, $\ell_i=(X_i-q_i)^2$ and $S_P(f)=\sum_i\mathbb E_P[f_C\ell_i]$. The allowance and [Multiword, Lemma 2.1][MW] give absolute convergence; [Conditional Response, Theorem 3.1][P8] gives $S_P(f)=0$ under attainment. The existing sufficient matrix condition for nullity is $\sum_{w\in B_L}f(w)M_w=0$ for this same presentation. With $I_R=[1-R,L+R]$ and

$$
q_{k,i}(P)=\mathbb E_P[X_i\mid X_{i-k:i-1},X_{i+1:i+k}],\qquad
U_{R,k}=\sum_{i\in I_R}\mathbb E_P[f_C(X_i-q_{k,i}(P))^2],
$$

same-law attainment implies the existing necessary bound

$$
|U_{R,k}|\le F\eta_\theta(R)
+2(L+2R)F\sqrt{\frac{c_\star}{k+1}}.
\tag{6.1}
$$

A strict violation with the supplied ceiling $\bar c=3-2\sqrt2$ replacing $c_\star$ certifies nonattainment of that same law. The finite statistic uses its actual marginal on $[1-R-k,L+R+k]$, with overlapping windows, legal seams, forced and zero-total fibers. The only supplied new input is the independently proved $\eta_\theta$; the finite-certificate proof is owned by [Multiword][MW].

If a candidate also has a nonzero complete response and a vanishing allowance, that existing theorem gives some finite violation. Synchronization and matrix-nullity alone give no nonzero response or productive sign. A pointwise allowance also does not supply [Multiword, Theorem 2.2][MW]'s separate common-tail and posterior-control hypotheses for a parameter family.

The existing four-state XOR tail obstruction forbids a fixed-$N$ uniform upgrade even within row-unifilar presentations. Its parameters $p_K=1/2+1/[16(K+1)]$, $K\ge1$, have

$$
e_L(r)+e_R(r)\ge2/9\quad(0\le r\le2K+1),\qquad
\tau_{P_K}(R)\ge\tfrac29(2K+2-R)\quad(R\le2K+1).
\tag{6.2}
$$

Each individual family member has a finite actual tail, including zero defects at its fair boundary, yet $\sup_{\theta\in\Theta_4}\tau_{P_\theta}(R)=\infty$ for every fixed $R$. This is the prior finite-hidden-tail obstruction, reused as a quantifier boundary rather than proved anew here. It neither supplies a fixed-law divergent actual tail nor refutes [Conditional Response, §2][P8]'s already proved attained-law budget $\tau_P(0)\le c_\star$.

